 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "grove",
   "title": "Into the mango grove",
   "time": "1:00, 23 June",
   "narrative": "After crossing the Bhagirathi on 22 June, Clive's little army marched through the wet night and reached Plassey about one in the morning. It took the Laksha Bagh, a walled and ditched mango grove roughly 730 metres long, and Clive made his quarters in the hunting lodge on the river bank just north of it. A mile off, behind earthworks that ran from the river and then swung north-east, the Nawab's huge army had been camped for more than a day.",
