  {
   "id": "sortie",
   "title": "The Nawab's army comes out",
   "time": "Dawn",
   "narrative": "At daybreak the Nawab's army left its camp and spread toward the grove. Sources count some 50,000 men and a very large park of heavy guns. Fifty French gunners under St. Frais took post at the larger tank with a few light pieces, within a mile of the British. Behind them stood the loyal general Mir Madan and the diwan Mohanlal with about 12,000 men. The rest formed a long arc: Rai Durlabh on the right, Yar Lutuf Khan in the centre and Mir Jafar, the secret ally of the British, on the left nearest Clive.",
