   "id": "line",
   "title": "The British line and the first shots",
   "time": "8:00",
   "narrative": "Clive watched from the roof of the lodge and ordered his men out of the grove to face the larger tank. The Europeans and topasses stood in the centre in four divisions with three six-pounders on each side, and the sepoys held the two wings. Two six-pounders and two howitzers were set behind brick kilns north of the left. At eight the French guns fired the first shot, killing a grenadier, and the whole Nawab's artillery opened a heavy and steady fire.",
