  {
   "id": "withdraw",
   "title": "Back behind the grove bank",
   "time": "8:30",
   "narrative": "Round shot from the Nawab's batteries mostly flew into his own cavalry and infantry, yet by half past eight the British had lost 10 Europeans and 20 sepoys. Clive pulled the main body back into the shelter of the grove, whose earth bank and ditch cut the casualty rate sharply. Only the advanced guns at the brick kilns stayed out to answer the French. For about three hours neither side changed position, and Clive's officers resolved to hold the grove until dark and attempt a night attack at midnight.",
