  {
   "id": "rain",
   "title": "Rain and the death of Mir Madan",
   "time": "c. 11:00-12:00",
   "narrative": "A heavy rainstorm broke over the field. Clive's gunners covered their powder with tarpaulins, but the Nawab's army took no such care and its powder was soaked. Supposing the British guns were dead too, Mir Madan led his cavalry in a charge as the rain eased. Grapeshot stopped it and mortally wounded him. The loss shook Siraj ud-Daulah, who in panic sought Mir Jafar's help, and Mir Jafar quietly passed the news to Clive and urged him to press forward.",
