   "narrative": "Rai Durlabh, the commander on the Nawab's right, advised Siraj to withdraw behind the entrenchment and to leave the fighting to his generals. The Nawab agreed. He ordered Mohanlal to pull back and then rode a camel toward Murshidabad with 2,000 horsemen. About two o'clock the army stopped its cannonade and began to turn north toward its camp, leaving St. Frais and his guns at the tank without support.",
