   "narrative": "Major Kilpatrick, left in command while Clive rested in the lodge, saw the Nawab's troops going away and saw that St. Frais was now alone. Without orders he took two companies of the 39th Foot and two field pieces toward the tank. Clive heard of it, hurried up, scolded him, and then brought out the rest of the army from the grove. Mir Jafar's division, trailing behind the Nawab's retiring columns, began to angle toward the grove.",
