  {
   "id": "cannonade",
   "title": "Bombarding the entrenchment",
   "time": "c. 15:00-16:00",
   "narrative": "From the mound of the larger tank the British guns fired into the Nawab's camp, and troops and guns that tried to come out were thrown into confusion. Clive sent half his force and guns to the smaller tank and the rest to a rise about 200 yards to its left. Matchlockmen fired from holes, ditches and bushes on the hill east of the redoubt, St. Frais kept his guns in the redoubt and the Nawab's horse charged more than once. This phase cost the British most of their casualties. Clive finally understood that the lingering division was Mir Jafar's.",
